 @engine`: `scan_axum_routes` (parsers/code/rust/src/lib.rs) finds `.route(` with string search over the whole file, so a test literal holding escaped Rust source (parsers/code/extractors/src/websocket.rs tests, engine/tests/http_qname_canonical.rs) is read as code and its escaped quote ends the path late. The Rust parser holds the file's tree, so the exact fix is AST-side: collect the byte ranges of `string_literal`, `raw_string_literal`, `char_literal`, `line_comment` and `block_comment` nodes once per file and refuse a needle whose first byte sits in one.

